WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.191 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.614
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.697 --> 00:32.241
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.366 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:36.620 --> 00:38.288
[Sejung's friend 1] It's someone
from her work.

00:38.372 --> 00:39.831
Sorry for this.

00:41.750 --> 00:42.876
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

00:42.960 --> 00:44.836
[♪ dreamy, ambient music playing]

00:51.343 --> 00:53.178
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

01:01.144 --> 01:02.229
Mr. Kim?

01:03.522 --> 01:04.564
[gasps softly]

01:05.524 --> 01:06.567
[gasps]

01:17.244 --> 01:19.663
Gosh, I'm sorry.

01:21.456 --> 01:23.250
[Sejung's friend 2] What's your problem?

01:23.333 --> 01:24.876
-Come on!
-What's your deal?

01:24.960 --> 01:26.044
Guys!

01:29.381 --> 01:30.716
[friends exclaiming excitedly]

01:30.799 --> 01:32.175
Was it your team leader?

01:32.259 --> 01:33.969
I couldn't tell from behind.

01:34.052 --> 01:36.054
-Let me see.
-Guys, stop it.

01:36.138 --> 01:39.349
Give the adults some alone time, will you?

01:39.433 --> 01:41.685
-I'm a grown-up, too.
-Let's go!

02:00.078 --> 02:02.581
They've probably left by now, right?

02:03.290 --> 02:05.125
-[♪ whimsical music playing]
-I suppose so.

02:06.752 --> 02:09.421
You have lipstick on your...

02:10.589 --> 02:11.757
No, the other side.

02:11.840 --> 02:13.342
Just a second.

02:14.968 --> 02:16.178
Right.

02:17.971 --> 02:19.056
We should hurry out.

02:19.139 --> 02:20.390
-Sure.
-Right.

02:20.474 --> 02:21.975
-After you.
-Right.

02:26.521 --> 02:27.606
Just a second.

02:38.825 --> 02:40.702
-Are they gone? Okay, let's go.
-Yes.

02:56.760 --> 02:58.762
Do you have a hammer?

02:59.304 --> 03:00.764
Just a second.

03:08.146 --> 03:10.774
A hammer?

03:11.608 --> 03:12.734
You don't have one?

03:13.402 --> 03:14.403
No.

03:15.862 --> 03:17.364
Oh, no.

03:20.784 --> 03:22.285
[♪ feel-good music playing]

03:24.830 --> 03:26.456
It should have everything you need.

03:26.540 --> 03:27.874
Right, thanks.

03:29.167 --> 03:30.460
How was your business trip?

03:32.796 --> 03:34.965
Oh, it went well.
I just got back yesterday.

03:35.048 --> 03:37.592
I heard you visited the house
while I was away.

03:37.676 --> 03:39.553
None of our stuff was organized,

03:39.636 --> 03:41.513
so it might have looked like
no one was living there.

03:41.596 --> 03:42.973
[chuckles]

03:43.056 --> 03:45.809
You must have some free time
since it's the weekend.

03:45.892 --> 03:47.144
Oh, right.

03:47.227 --> 03:49.020
My husband is extremely busy.

03:49.104 --> 03:51.565
Even I can't get a hold of him
on weekdays. [chuckles]

03:51.648 --> 03:53.567
Sweetie, don't take on too much work.

03:53.650 --> 03:55.193
It'll cost you your health.

03:55.277 --> 03:57.737
I've been working out,
so don't worry, sweetie.

03:57.821 --> 03:59.823
-Got it, sweetie.
-Sure.

03:59.906 --> 04:01.074
[chuckles]

04:01.450 --> 04:02.617
Are you going to work out?

04:02.701 --> 04:05.412
I was planning to play some squash.
Would you like to join me?

04:05.871 --> 04:08.874
I'm afraid we already have plans.

04:08.957 --> 04:12.419
We had to call it off once before,
so we can't do that again.

04:12.502 --> 04:15.005
That's right. We already have plans.

04:15.088 --> 04:17.674
-What a bummer.
-[both chuckle softly]

04:18.592 --> 04:20.469
[♪ whimsical music playing]

04:20.552 --> 04:22.429
Sure, we can hang out next time.

04:22.512 --> 04:23.972
Got it.

04:24.055 --> 04:26.600
[closes gate]

04:31.271 --> 04:33.023
-Is this really necessary?
-[sighs]

04:33.106 --> 04:34.983
Don't you know
offense is the best defense?

04:35.066 --> 04:36.985
He was clearly suspicious last time.

04:37.068 --> 04:39.029
With you gone... What are you doing?

04:39.112 --> 04:40.113
He's watching us.

04:40.822 --> 04:42.491
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

04:44.326 --> 04:45.327
He really is.

04:51.208 --> 04:52.918
-Shall we?
-Sure.

04:56.254 --> 04:58.089
Is this absolutely necessary?

04:58.173 --> 05:00.467
[Kim Wooju] I thought offense
was the best defense.

05:00.550 --> 05:01.676
[Meri chuckles] True.

05:03.136 --> 05:04.554
Slow down, will you?

05:04.638 --> 05:06.097
Walk faster.

05:06.181 --> 05:08.975
My slipper's slipping off.

05:09.392 --> 05:11.394
[Kim Wooju] That belongs in the trash.

05:11.478 --> 05:13.230
[Meri] Now you're just being mean.

05:13.313 --> 05:15.690
These are my comfort slippers.

05:15.774 --> 05:17.067
Geez.

05:19.027 --> 05:20.904
Why is he still watching us?
[giggles]

05:21.321 --> 05:22.531
[Kim Wooju sighs]

05:25.534 --> 05:26.827
-Is he still looking?
-Mmm-hmm.

05:27.536 --> 05:28.787
[both chuckle]

05:30.080 --> 05:32.374
My lips are trembling
from all this smiling.

05:32.457 --> 05:33.500
[sighs in relief]

05:34.626 --> 05:37.546
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

05:37.629 --> 05:39.548
EPISODE 4

05:40.173 --> 05:41.550
[Ms. Oh] Right here,

05:41.633 --> 05:44.135
you can see the sales
from last year's holiday season.

05:44.219 --> 05:49.474
These were a huge hit
because of the duty-free promotional deal.

05:50.100 --> 05:52.227
That's good to hear.
I'll make a copy of this.

05:52.310 --> 05:53.645
No, let me.

05:53.728 --> 05:55.647
I'm good, but thanks.

05:59.693 --> 06:00.861
[sighs]

06:00.944 --> 06:02.529
[♪ dramatic music playing]

06:04.030 --> 06:05.282
I know it was him.

06:09.202 --> 06:10.537
-What do you mean?
-[gasps]

06:12.330 --> 06:13.874
-Did that hurt?
-[groans]

06:14.749 --> 06:16.918
What were you going on about?

06:18.628 --> 06:20.213
It definitely looked like him.

06:20.297 --> 06:22.048
I'm sure you saw someone similar.

06:22.132 --> 06:23.884
Why would Mr. Kim go there?

06:24.718 --> 06:26.761
Enjoy. Here you go.

06:26.845 --> 06:30.015
The company cafe serves
great coffee with quality beans.

06:30.098 --> 06:32.601
-Gosh, thanks.
-Thank you.

06:32.684 --> 06:33.852
What was that?

06:33.935 --> 06:34.936
Where did you see Mr. Kim?

06:35.020 --> 06:38.481
Sejung saw Mr. Kim
at a self-service photo studio.

06:38.565 --> 06:40.233
-[coughs]
-[Sejung] Do you know the place

06:40.317 --> 06:42.485
at the intersection
that offers 50 percent off?

06:42.569 --> 06:44.905
-I went there with my friends last weekend
-[Meri coughs]

06:44.988 --> 06:48.950
and saw someone who looked like Mr. Kim
taking wedding photos.

06:49.034 --> 06:50.076
Wedding photos?

06:50.160 --> 06:52.454
[clears throat] You must've been mistaken.
[chuckles nervously]

06:52.537 --> 06:53.872
Exactly.

06:53.955 --> 06:55.540
Why would Mr. Kim go there?

06:55.624 --> 06:56.750
He doesn't have a girlfriend.

06:56.833 --> 06:59.044
[Sejung] It seemed
like a themed photo shoot,

06:59.127 --> 07:01.630
but the guy looked exactly
like Mr. Kim from behind.

07:01.713 --> 07:04.466
-Tall with a petite head.
-[Wonseok] A petite head.

07:04.549 --> 07:06.009
[Sejung] His hair had two parts.

07:06.092 --> 07:08.303
My hair also has two parts.

07:08.386 --> 07:09.679
See?

07:09.763 --> 07:10.889
Go away!

07:10.972 --> 07:12.724
-Did you see the woman?
-[Sejung] Sorry?

07:12.807 --> 07:15.435
If it was a wedding photo,
there would've been a girl.

07:15.518 --> 07:17.228
-What did she look like?
-[exclaims]

07:17.312 --> 07:18.521
[gulps]

07:18.605 --> 07:19.939
[Sejung hums thoughtfully]

07:20.023 --> 07:21.191
[clicks tongue]

07:22.651 --> 07:24.194
[♪ upbeat dramatic music playing]

07:25.695 --> 07:26.863
[exclaims softly]

07:26.946 --> 07:28.073
She was a lot like you.

07:32.827 --> 07:34.788
She had a figure
similar to yours, Ms. Yoo.

07:35.997 --> 07:37.749
The height and everything.

07:39.042 --> 07:40.168
She was just like you.

07:43.171 --> 07:44.547
You should've seen her face.

07:44.631 --> 07:46.925
Her face? Well...

07:47.008 --> 07:49.511
I couldn't because they were kissing.

07:52.055 --> 07:53.765
-Were they kissing?
-[Sejung] Yes.

07:53.848 --> 07:56.267
Their lips were locked.

07:56.351 --> 07:59.270
Why don't you check with the photo studio?

08:00.438 --> 08:02.315
Check who reserved that time slot.

08:02.649 --> 08:04.609
[Ms. Oh gasps] Ms. Shin, you genius!

08:05.276 --> 08:08.655
You're right. Why didn't I think of that?

08:10.115 --> 08:11.825
I have the studio's number on my phone.

08:11.908 --> 08:13.785
-[Wonseok] Give them a call.
-Wait.

08:14.244 --> 08:15.745
-Here we go.
-I don't think...

08:15.829 --> 08:18.748
I don't think they will share
personal information.

08:19.457 --> 08:21.960
Hello, is this
the self-service photo studio?

08:22.961 --> 08:25.046
I was hoping to ask you something.

08:25.130 --> 08:26.423
Ms. Cha!

08:26.506 --> 08:28.091
I have something to ask.

08:28.842 --> 08:30.468
Shall we begin the meeting?

08:30.552 --> 08:32.721
-Ms. Yoo.
-[Meri] I have something to say.

08:32.804 --> 08:34.389
-I mean, ask...
-[Sejung] What was that?

08:34.472 --> 08:36.516
I can't quite hear you.

08:37.600 --> 08:40.770
[Ms. Oh] Ms. Yoo,
can I have your attention?

08:40.854 --> 08:43.773
I had the reservation
put under a different name just in case.

08:43.857 --> 08:44.983
Tosun, to be exact.

08:45.900 --> 08:47.068
[sighs in relief]

08:47.861 --> 08:49.696
Couldn't you have told me that?

08:49.779 --> 08:51.072
I was sweating in there.

08:51.156 --> 08:54.325
That's your fault for booking a studio
close to the office.

08:54.409 --> 08:56.369
People could've seen us.

08:56.870 --> 08:59.205
I thought it would be safer
near the office

08:59.289 --> 09:01.249
because it was the weekend.

09:02.083 --> 09:04.169
Anyway, I'm sorry. I'll be more careful.

09:05.128 --> 09:08.548
-Has Mr. Baek reached out since that day?
-No.

09:08.631 --> 09:11.176
I'm going to cancel the home visit
as soon as I can.

09:11.885 --> 09:13.011
How?

09:13.762 --> 09:14.929
[hums thoughtfully]

09:15.013 --> 09:18.183
We could be in a car accident,
or a family member could die.

09:18.725 --> 09:21.144
Wow, you lie like nobody's business.

09:21.227 --> 09:22.854
Avoiding him should be a priority.

09:22.937 --> 09:25.398
Things won't go well for you
if I get caught.

09:26.566 --> 09:28.401
-Are you blackmailing me?
-Of course not!

09:29.402 --> 09:31.279
Is that how I came off?

09:31.362 --> 09:35.241
It's just that
I didn't want to put you out anymore.

09:36.076 --> 09:39.037
The wedding photos we took together
were more than enough.

09:39.996 --> 09:40.997
Ah!

09:42.165 --> 09:43.208
The wedding photos...

09:43.291 --> 09:44.459
You know,

09:45.251 --> 09:47.253
I'm only saying this just in case.

09:47.962 --> 09:51.132
I hope you don't read too much into it.

09:51.716 --> 09:52.759
A modeling gig.

09:52.842 --> 09:55.220
Just think of it as that.

09:55.303 --> 10:00.058
[scoffs] I'm sorry to say this,
but that's how I've always seen it.

10:01.101 --> 10:03.144
You seem to be reading
more into it than I am.

10:03.228 --> 10:04.646
-Me?
-It looked like

10:04.729 --> 10:08.149
you were getting what you want
by pretending it's for wedding photos.

10:08.900 --> 10:11.361
You caught me off guard
by swooping in like that.

10:12.153 --> 10:14.072
-I swooped in?
-[♪ upbeat dramatic music playing]

10:14.155 --> 10:15.573
Mr. Kim?

10:17.617 --> 10:18.701
[Sejung gasps]

10:22.163 --> 10:24.624
I was simply worried she'd catch us.

10:24.707 --> 10:28.002
It definitely felt like
I locked eyes with Sejung.

10:28.086 --> 10:29.337
Besides, the kiss?

10:29.838 --> 10:31.089
You started it.

10:31.172 --> 10:33.424
I never meant for things to go that far.

10:33.508 --> 10:36.928
All I wanted to do was
to get us into a certain pose.

10:37.011 --> 10:40.265
But all of a sudden,
you came at me like a bull...

10:40.348 --> 10:42.392
[scoffs] "Like a bull"?

10:42.475 --> 10:44.435
You've got to be kidding me.

10:44.519 --> 10:48.982
Just know that I wasn't trying to get
anything from you.

10:51.526 --> 10:53.278
What was that look just now?

10:53.361 --> 10:54.445
Don't you believe me?

10:54.529 --> 10:56.156
[♪ dramatic sting]

10:57.490 --> 10:58.741
[hesitates]

10:58.825 --> 10:59.909
Whatever.

11:00.869 --> 11:02.078
Here.

11:02.787 --> 11:04.330
I got you some clothes and shoes.

11:05.331 --> 11:07.584
I actually needed these. [gasps]

11:08.042 --> 11:09.752
No way. Even your underwear?

11:11.129 --> 11:12.881
You're good with details, aren't you?

11:12.964 --> 11:14.924
That's how you get work done.

11:15.008 --> 11:17.093
Meticulously, without missing a detail.

11:18.344 --> 11:19.762
Consider me schooled.

11:20.430 --> 11:22.056
Return the favor with good work.

11:24.350 --> 11:27.145
The chairwoman liked the design proposal.

11:27.645 --> 11:29.480
She wants to hear from you in person.

11:29.856 --> 11:31.316
Really?

11:32.025 --> 11:33.276
Hold on a second.

11:33.359 --> 11:35.320
If they like this new design,

11:35.403 --> 11:39.908
could they ask us to update the packaging
for their current products?

11:39.991 --> 11:41.284
Yes.

11:41.367 --> 11:44.078
Think of the range of products
Myungsoondang has.

11:44.162 --> 11:46.581
We'll tackle this project
like it's do or die.

11:46.664 --> 11:48.750
Don't pop the champagne too soon.

11:49.167 --> 11:52.003
Myungsoondang's chairwoman is no joke.

11:52.086 --> 11:53.087
How so?

11:53.171 --> 11:57.467
-Isn't she the founder's daughter-in-law?
-She is.

11:57.550 --> 12:02.263
She took the small steamed bun shop
her mother-in-law ran at the market

12:02.347 --> 12:05.350
and turned it into the Myungsoondang
we know today.

12:05.433 --> 12:06.684
Despite being over 70,

12:06.768 --> 12:10.647
she visits the factory every morning
and samples every product.

12:10.730 --> 12:13.608
She also looks after the health
and well-being of her bakers.

12:13.691 --> 12:14.776
That's admirable.

12:15.318 --> 12:17.528
-[exclaims quizzically]
-I want the job even more now.

12:17.612 --> 12:19.864
People like her
tend to stay loyal, you know.

12:19.948 --> 12:21.741
They never change
their view of you, either.

12:21.824 --> 12:22.951
That's true.

12:24.452 --> 12:25.578
It's settled.

12:25.662 --> 12:26.955
I'm pulling all-nighters.

12:27.038 --> 12:29.123
I'll be ready with even Plans B and C.

12:32.001 --> 12:34.128
Did everything go smoothly at the funeral?

12:34.212 --> 12:37.090
Yes, the ceremony was simple
because he had a small family.

12:37.173 --> 12:38.424
You did well.

12:38.508 --> 12:41.302
I talked to Mr. Ko's wife this morning.

12:42.845 --> 12:44.681
He was still quite young.

12:47.183 --> 12:50.645
Assist the family
in any way the company can.

12:51.020 --> 12:52.939
Maybe find a job for his wife
in the company.

12:53.773 --> 12:57.777
Of course. However,
there's something I must report.

12:59.320 --> 13:01.447
It seems like Mr. Ko

13:02.073 --> 13:04.075
was embezzling company money.

13:05.410 --> 13:06.577
What are you talking about?

13:06.661 --> 13:09.038
The internal audit team caught him
the day before the accident.

13:09.122 --> 13:10.123
When questioned,

13:10.873 --> 13:12.292
he admitted to gambling.

13:12.375 --> 13:13.668
[♪ tense, melancholy music playing]

13:13.751 --> 13:16.587
He promised to pay the money back
with his severance after retiring,

13:17.922 --> 13:19.215
but then the accident happened.

13:19.716 --> 13:20.758
Gambling?

13:22.468 --> 13:24.679
[sighs] He wouldn't have.

13:25.346 --> 13:27.307
[sighs] I couldn't believe it, either,

13:28.099 --> 13:30.977
but you never really know people.

13:31.936 --> 13:33.021
[sighs softly]

13:33.980 --> 13:36.399
He took a sizable amount,
so what should we do?

13:36.816 --> 13:40.820
If we file a police report,
the press could get wind of it.

13:41.988 --> 13:43.489
What do you think we should do?

13:44.323 --> 13:48.494
It's wrong to speak ill of the dead,
and he was a loyal employee,

13:48.578 --> 13:50.538
so I believe
it'd be wise to keep this quiet.

13:54.375 --> 13:55.668
[♪ ominous sting]

13:58.921 --> 14:03.259
For now, Eungsoo will fill in for Mr. Ko.

14:03.634 --> 14:04.761
What?

14:04.844 --> 14:05.928
Me?

14:06.012 --> 14:08.389
Accounting really isn't my strong suit.

14:08.473 --> 14:11.350
This will just be a temporary role
until we hire someone.

14:11.851 --> 14:13.895
I'll supervise the team myself,
so don't worry.

14:13.978 --> 14:16.481
I'd feel better knowing
you'll be taking charge.

14:17.023 --> 14:18.941
You could show Eungsoo
how the work is done.

14:19.025 --> 14:20.026
Sure.

14:20.985 --> 14:22.278
I'll get back to my meal.

14:24.072 --> 14:26.783
[sighs] Talk about a bomb going off.

14:27.950 --> 14:30.787
Mr. Ko and his wife
even had a meal here with us once.

14:30.870 --> 14:31.871
Right?

14:32.455 --> 14:36.250
They were excited to win a vacation
for his long service to the company.

14:36.334 --> 14:38.044
You should always drive carefully.

14:38.127 --> 14:39.754
He's lucky it was just him.

14:39.837 --> 14:41.297
What if his family were with him?

14:41.380 --> 14:43.007
They'd all have been killed--

14:43.091 --> 14:44.092
Honey.

14:44.175 --> 14:45.218
What?

14:45.760 --> 14:47.720
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

14:53.434 --> 14:54.435
Come on.

14:55.770 --> 14:57.647
We all know the story, don't we?

14:57.730 --> 14:59.857
It shouldn't really be taboo
in the family.

15:02.568 --> 15:05.822
Wooju, I wasn't trying to upset you.

15:06.781 --> 15:08.241
-I'm fine.
-[acknowledges]

15:22.130 --> 15:23.214
[clears throat]

15:24.590 --> 15:26.092
I'd like to excuse myself.

15:35.393 --> 15:37.603
Didn't he like the food? [clears throat]
He must be picky.

15:37.687 --> 15:39.772
[loudly] You blabbermouth!

15:40.189 --> 15:41.691
Eat with a mask on.

15:42.066 --> 15:43.693
Then how would I be able to eat?

15:43.776 --> 15:45.486
Just shut your mouth

15:45.570 --> 15:47.488
and stop talking nonsense
at the dinner table.

15:47.572 --> 15:49.198
You always pick on me.

15:49.282 --> 15:50.867
Wooju said he was fine.

15:50.950 --> 15:52.743
[Eungsoo] Mom, he isn't fine.

15:52.827 --> 15:54.370
People rarely know this,

15:54.453 --> 15:57.290
but Wooju is more fainthearted
than he seems

15:57.373 --> 15:59.250
and gets scared easily.

16:00.376 --> 16:01.752
[clears throat] When he was little,

16:01.836 --> 16:04.672
he stayed in his room
and clutched his stuffed toy

16:04.755 --> 16:06.048
whenever thunder struck.
[chortles]

16:06.132 --> 16:07.300
-His toy?
-[Eungsoo] Yes.

16:07.383 --> 16:08.926
I don't know where he found it,

16:09.635 --> 16:10.970
but it became his comfort toy.

16:13.389 --> 16:14.473
[sighs in exasperation]

16:14.557 --> 16:16.225
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

16:51.969 --> 16:53.012
[sighs softly]

17:26.921 --> 17:28.923
[young Kim Wooju] Help.

17:29.757 --> 17:31.676
Please help.

17:32.218 --> 17:33.928
Help...

17:34.554 --> 17:35.930
[tires screech]

17:36.514 --> 17:37.598
[gasps, panting]

17:37.682 --> 17:38.683
Are you okay?

17:40.518 --> 17:42.019
What on earth?

17:42.812 --> 17:44.063
[crying]

17:45.606 --> 17:48.234
-I was driving from that direction...
-[young Kim Wooju] Dad!

17:48.317 --> 17:49.318
...when I saw him

17:49.402 --> 17:51.696
-standing on the road looking like that.
-Mom!

17:52.280 --> 17:53.281
Dad!

17:53.364 --> 17:55.825
[taxi driver] Then I found the car
and his parents thrown over there.

17:55.908 --> 17:57.034
[young Kim Wooju] Mom!

17:57.868 --> 17:59.829
-[taxi driver] It's a miracle he survived.
-[crying]

18:00.329 --> 18:02.582
-[officer] On the road?
-[taxi driver tsk-tsks sadly]

18:02.665 --> 18:04.917
You were driving your taxi
down Route Three

18:05.001 --> 18:06.002
when you saw the boy.

18:06.085 --> 18:07.086
That's right.

18:11.215 --> 18:13.092
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

18:26.689 --> 18:27.940
Take it.

18:28.441 --> 18:30.401
My dad gave it to me as a birthday gift.

18:33.821 --> 18:37.825
[teddy] Enough with the tears,
or the tiger will come and get you.

18:38.868 --> 18:40.077
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

18:45.708 --> 18:46.917
Wooju!

18:47.418 --> 18:49.420
Grandma!

18:49.837 --> 18:51.547
[crying] Grandma...

18:53.299 --> 18:54.550
Grandma...

18:54.634 --> 18:55.760
Are you all right?

19:06.646 --> 19:08.606
[taxi driver] Why are you crying,
sweet pea?

19:08.689 --> 19:09.857
[young girl crying] Dad.

19:09.940 --> 19:12.568
Did his mom and dad both die?

19:12.652 --> 19:14.278
[taxi driver] Of course not.

19:14.862 --> 19:15.988
They will be fine.

19:16.405 --> 19:18.991
What if they both die?

19:19.408 --> 19:22.244
That poor boy!

19:22.912 --> 19:24.747
-[♪ melancholy music playing]
-Come here.

19:26.165 --> 19:29.001
Who will take care of him?

19:29.794 --> 19:32.380
That poor boy!

19:33.381 --> 19:35.132
[young girl continues crying]

19:41.764 --> 19:45.768
[teddy] Enough with the tears,
or the tiger will come and get you.

19:52.483 --> 19:54.568
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

20:00.074 --> 20:01.242
Sorry for this.

20:01.617 --> 20:03.452
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

20:04.870 --> 20:06.455
Why are you still thinking about him?

20:06.539 --> 20:08.332
It's not like the kiss was real.

20:08.749 --> 20:11.752
All I wanted to do was
to get us into a certain pose.

20:11.836 --> 20:15.548
But all of a sudden,
you came at me like a bull...

20:19.927 --> 20:22.388
I didn't even use my tongue.

20:22.471 --> 20:23.681
[Sejung] Mr. Kim?

20:23.806 --> 20:24.890
[gasps softly]

20:25.182 --> 20:26.350
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

20:27.518 --> 20:29.061
Or did I?

20:33.566 --> 20:34.859
Hold on.

20:35.401 --> 20:36.610
I was like...

20:49.749 --> 20:50.875
Have you lost it?

20:53.419 --> 20:55.212
Did I get too into character?

20:58.424 --> 20:59.467
No way.

20:59.550 --> 21:00.676
There's no way.

21:00.760 --> 21:02.928
That's absurd.

21:03.012 --> 21:04.805
[♪ upbeat music playing]

21:08.142 --> 21:09.143
[whines]

21:15.191 --> 21:16.275
[exclaims]

21:19.320 --> 21:22.865
[Jingyeong]
"A good place to confess your feelings."

21:25.659 --> 21:28.204
A GOOD PLACE TO CONFESS YOUR FEELINGS

21:36.212 --> 21:37.505
[Jingyeong over phone] Hey, Wooju.

21:37.588 --> 21:38.756
What are you up to this evening?

21:38.839 --> 21:40.466
-[Kim Wooju] This evening?
-Yes.

21:40.549 --> 21:42.218
I get off work early today.

21:42.760 --> 21:45.638
It'd be a crime to go straight home
on a day like this.

21:45.721 --> 21:48.849
Don't you have
other friends to hang out with?

21:48.933 --> 21:50.351
Are you a loner at work?

21:50.434 --> 21:52.603
I was worried you'd be bored.

21:53.354 --> 21:54.939
So much for going someplace nice.

21:55.022 --> 21:56.232
Forget it.

21:56.315 --> 21:58.108
Okay, fine.

21:58.192 --> 22:01.362
I have plans during the day,
so I'll see you this evening.

22:01.987 --> 22:04.156
Okay, call me when you're done.

22:05.074 --> 22:06.158
Sure.

22:07.701 --> 22:08.702
[line disconnects]

22:09.370 --> 22:11.914
Dr. Yoon, are you going on a date?

22:12.373 --> 22:14.375
She definitely looks
like she's going on one.

22:14.458 --> 22:15.459
What?

22:19.046 --> 22:21.215
Have you taken the VIP patient

22:21.298 --> 22:23.050
-Lee Sungwoo's blood pressure?
-Yes.

22:23.133 --> 22:25.052
But I don't think it was necessary.

22:25.135 --> 22:28.556
He almost bit my head off
for interrupting his sleep.

22:28.639 --> 22:30.516
That's one annoying little--

22:37.857 --> 22:39.733
I feel bad for that guy.

22:39.817 --> 22:42.403
He has to come
whenever he's summoned, day or night.

22:47.074 --> 22:48.701
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

23:26.238 --> 23:28.115
That should do it.

23:28.198 --> 23:30.784
Anyone would think
that a newlywed couple lives here.

23:32.369 --> 23:34.455
-Are you done changing?
-[Kim Wooju] Yes.

23:37.041 --> 23:39.501
Is this really necessary?

23:39.585 --> 23:42.212
All newlyweds wear matching clothes.

23:42.880 --> 23:44.006
Are you cool or warm-toned?

23:44.089 --> 23:45.299
It looks good on you.

23:47.009 --> 23:48.177
Just a second.

23:52.932 --> 23:55.059
I guess I don't look so bad.

24:02.149 --> 24:03.943
[♪ whimsical music playing]

24:05.277 --> 24:06.362
[chuckles softly]

24:07.404 --> 24:08.697
Here.

24:08.781 --> 24:10.491
Are you kidding me?

24:10.574 --> 24:13.786
If we're doing this,
we might as well make it perfect.

24:16.997 --> 24:19.792
Did you have me come early
so you could dress me up?

24:19.875 --> 24:21.794
There's still a lot of time.

24:22.252 --> 24:24.254
That's only one of the reasons.

24:24.338 --> 24:27.174
We have things to get ready
before people get here.

24:28.384 --> 24:29.635
Pop quiz!

24:31.762 --> 24:33.514
When's our wedding anniversary?

24:33.597 --> 24:34.598
January 6.

24:35.599 --> 24:37.017
You have a good memory.

24:37.101 --> 24:38.852
That was barely a quiz.

24:38.936 --> 24:40.229
Where was our honeymoon?

24:41.188 --> 24:43.023
Well? That's...

24:43.107 --> 24:44.358
I never told you.

24:44.441 --> 24:46.777
-Geez, no wonder.
-Here you go.

24:46.860 --> 24:48.988
I put together questions people could ask.

24:49.822 --> 24:51.073
Take a look.

24:51.657 --> 24:52.992
[inhales sharply]

24:53.283 --> 24:54.368
[exhales]

24:55.244 --> 24:56.745
2. HONEYMOON TRIP?
LONDON, UK

24:56.829 --> 24:58.163
POTENTIAL QUESTIONS

24:58.247 --> 24:59.248
[Kim Wooju] London?

24:59.331 --> 25:01.542
Did you plan to go to London
for your honeymoon?

25:01.625 --> 25:04.420
-Yes, to see Son Heungmin play.
-I see.

25:04.503 --> 25:05.587
Do you like soccer?

25:05.671 --> 25:07.798
No, I just like Son Heungmin.
I'm clueless about soccer.

25:08.257 --> 25:09.341
[chuckles softly]

25:09.800 --> 25:11.010
Man.

25:11.093 --> 25:13.595
Your ex-fiancé was a generous man.

25:13.679 --> 25:17.391
He was letting his girlfriend
see another man during your honeymoon.

25:17.975 --> 25:19.018
[acknowledges]

25:20.144 --> 25:24.481
I used 10 years' worth of my mileage
to pay for our round-trip tickets.

25:24.565 --> 25:26.984
That's why I got to choose
the destination.

25:27.901 --> 25:30.612
Did you pay for the honeymoon as well?

25:30.696 --> 25:32.197
You also paid for the apartment.

25:32.781 --> 25:36.201
I paid his tuition twice,
arranged his insurance,

25:36.285 --> 25:38.912
and paid for his TOEIC classes.

25:39.246 --> 25:40.539
[gasps in awe]

25:41.165 --> 25:44.126
It's fair since I was
the first to earn money.

25:44.209 --> 25:46.086
He didn't have any money saved up.

25:46.628 --> 25:48.338
Whoever has the money should pay.

25:48.422 --> 25:51.800
Then, did he even thank you?

25:54.428 --> 25:55.471
[hesitates]

25:58.098 --> 26:00.184
I guess he didn't.

26:05.939 --> 26:08.525
How on earth did you two meet?

26:09.068 --> 26:11.320
While on vacation with my friends.

26:11.403 --> 26:13.113
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

26:17.034 --> 26:18.035
[friend 1] Meri!

26:18.118 --> 26:19.369
[friend 2] Yoo Meri!

26:19.453 --> 26:21.497
-Right here.
-Over there.

26:22.247 --> 26:23.665
-Hurry.
-[friend 1] Oh, no.

26:23.749 --> 26:24.958
[friend 2] Meri!

26:25.042 --> 26:26.376
Hold on.

26:26.460 --> 26:28.837
-[friend 1] Please.
-[friend 2] Please open your eyes.

26:28.921 --> 26:30.631
[friend 1] Are you okay?

26:30.714 --> 26:32.674
-[coughs]
-[friend 1] Can you get up?

26:32.758 --> 26:34.259
[friend 2] Meri, are you okay?

26:35.260 --> 26:37.971
[Meri] I was drowning in the water,

26:38.597 --> 26:42.059
and I woke up
to a hottie looking down at me.

26:48.065 --> 26:49.483
You fell for his looks.

26:49.566 --> 26:51.777
[chuckles] I guess.

26:52.694 --> 26:58.158
But no one decides to marry someone
just for his looks.

27:00.786 --> 27:02.162
[paper rustles]

27:02.746 --> 27:03.747
Do you regret it?

27:05.874 --> 27:08.043
Do I regret it?

27:09.002 --> 27:10.087
I did.

27:11.839 --> 27:15.467
Why did I give him
every piece of my heart?

27:15.551 --> 27:16.927
What a fool.

27:19.555 --> 27:22.432
That's what I thought love was.

27:25.310 --> 27:27.354
I'm done with that now.

27:28.272 --> 27:29.481
Come on.

27:29.565 --> 27:31.650
Why do you need to change?

27:32.734 --> 27:33.902
I'm sure

27:34.778 --> 27:38.782
you'll meet someone
who won't take your love for granted.

27:39.575 --> 27:41.159
[♪ soft piano music playing]

27:42.494 --> 27:44.246
Will that day come?

27:47.833 --> 27:48.959
Just so you know,

27:50.502 --> 27:52.170
that was very comforting.

27:53.839 --> 27:55.048
[chuckles softly]

28:02.556 --> 28:03.891
[phone vibrating]

28:07.686 --> 28:10.856
MOM

28:11.523 --> 28:13.859
[automated voice] The call cannot
be connected. Transferring to...

28:13.942 --> 28:16.528
Could she be busy?

28:19.156 --> 28:20.699
-Seriously, Sunja?
-Oh, it's hot.

28:20.782 --> 28:22.367
Eat it all, why don't you?

28:22.451 --> 28:25.370
The person this food is for
hasn't even eaten any yet.

28:25.454 --> 28:28.874
No need to be stingy
when you made so much.

28:28.957 --> 28:30.167
By the way,

28:30.250 --> 28:32.461
are Meri's future in-laws
throwing a feast?

28:32.544 --> 28:33.754
Not really.

28:33.837 --> 28:36.340
I'm going to drop some off
since I'm heading to Seoul

28:36.423 --> 28:37.883
to visit my aunt in the hospital.

28:37.966 --> 28:40.594
Oh, lucky them.

28:40.677 --> 28:42.304
If I had a son,

28:42.387 --> 28:44.890
I'd happily let him marry
one of your daughters.

28:44.973 --> 28:49.311
That would mean enjoying
all this tasty food every season.

28:49.394 --> 28:50.562
[both chuckle]

28:50.646 --> 28:52.814
Like I'd let my girls marry just anyone.

28:52.898 --> 28:55.859
Meri's fiancé's dad
is a college professor.

28:55.943 --> 28:57.069
So?

28:57.152 --> 28:58.612
That same educated family

28:58.695 --> 29:02.324
hasn't even said thank you
for all the food you've given them.

29:02.407 --> 29:04.242
After you receive, you should give.

29:04.326 --> 29:05.661
Talk about being rude.

29:05.744 --> 29:07.162
I've been turning them down.

29:07.245 --> 29:09.206
This is nothing to brag about.

29:09.289 --> 29:14.252
Anyone can tell
they look down on you, except you.

29:14.336 --> 29:18.882
On top of that, your future son-in-law
never even visited once.

29:18.966 --> 29:20.300
He's busy, that's why.

29:20.384 --> 29:21.635
He doesn't lounge around all day.

29:21.718 --> 29:24.221
He works for a big
investment company in Seoul.

29:24.304 --> 29:26.640
Like you know anything.

29:26.723 --> 29:29.309
I refused when they asked me
to live with them in Seoul.

29:29.810 --> 29:30.852
Really?

29:30.936 --> 29:31.937
That's right.

29:32.312 --> 29:35.816
He's been telling me to call him
if I'm ever in Seoul.

29:35.899 --> 29:38.485
You know what?
I should ask him to get together tomorrow.

29:38.568 --> 29:40.195
-Go ahead.
-My son-in-law.

29:40.278 --> 29:41.613
MY SON-IN-LAW

29:41.697 --> 29:43.156
[shower running]

29:47.327 --> 29:48.495
[sighs in exasperation]

29:50.956 --> 29:53.959
I thought it hit the lowest point,
but there was worse to come.

29:55.711 --> 29:58.130
Why are only my shares dropping in price?

29:58.839 --> 30:01.883
When will you go up? Will you ever go up?

30:01.967 --> 30:02.968
MERI'S MOTHER

30:03.051 --> 30:04.386
[♪ ominous sting]

30:07.347 --> 30:08.932
-Why is she calling me?
-[phone vibrating]

30:09.016 --> 30:10.517
[♪ dramatic music playing]

30:11.435 --> 30:13.687
Meri told me to keep quiet
for the time being.

30:14.771 --> 30:16.356
Does she know?

30:20.277 --> 30:21.319
Damn it.

30:21.862 --> 30:22.946
[sighs]

30:30.287 --> 30:31.329
[phone vibrates]

30:31.413 --> 30:33.206
C: I'M IN ROOM 3613

30:40.964 --> 30:41.965
"C"?

30:42.049 --> 30:43.216
[shower stops]

30:49.097 --> 30:50.599
C: I'M IN ROOM 3613

30:51.516 --> 30:52.726
[Jenny] Wooju.

30:54.352 --> 30:55.479
Hit the shower.

30:59.691 --> 31:00.901
I won't be long.

31:00.984 --> 31:02.319
[giggles] Sure.

31:16.917 --> 31:18.001
Yes, Ms. Yoo.

31:19.669 --> 31:22.172
I'm afraid I'll have to cancel
the home visit today.

31:22.255 --> 31:24.591
Something urgent came up for my boss.

31:25.258 --> 31:26.384
I'm really sorry.

31:26.885 --> 31:29.137
Please tell your husband how sorry I am.

31:30.138 --> 31:31.139
Take care.

31:31.223 --> 31:32.432
[line disconnects]

31:36.394 --> 31:37.687
[stutters]

31:37.771 --> 31:39.731
See? I was right!

31:39.815 --> 31:42.067
Seriously, the guy's a lunatic.

31:42.150 --> 31:44.778
He started punching me
for just looking at him.

31:44.861 --> 31:46.279
Oh, geez.

31:46.363 --> 31:48.323
I make my living with my face.

31:48.406 --> 31:51.243
How can this fly here?
[exclaiming in pain]

31:51.326 --> 31:52.744
[Sanghyeon] Are you Mr. Kim Gusik?

31:54.704 --> 31:55.705
Who are you?

31:56.706 --> 31:58.333
I represent Mr. Lee Sungwoo.

31:59.751 --> 32:00.752
We should talk.

32:00.836 --> 32:02.087
MANAGING DIRECTOR
BAEK SANGHYEON

32:02.170 --> 32:04.422
You want me to say I assaulted him, too?

32:04.923 --> 32:06.049
[chuckles]

32:06.133 --> 32:07.175
What a joke.

32:07.259 --> 32:09.845
Mister, there's video evidence.

32:11.721 --> 32:13.473
The security footage will be deleted,

32:14.015 --> 32:19.020
but you'll find money in your bank account
you never imagined having.

32:19.104 --> 32:20.272
As if.

32:22.524 --> 32:24.276
Would this be enough?

32:28.155 --> 32:29.573
300,000,000 WON

32:29.656 --> 32:31.241
[♪ dramatic sting]

32:33.243 --> 32:35.620
Why did he suddenly cancel? What for?

32:36.204 --> 32:37.581
Beats me.

32:37.664 --> 32:39.416
I don't mind avoiding the guy, but...

32:40.167 --> 32:42.377
You went through all this trouble
for nothing.

32:42.460 --> 32:44.254
Oh, it's fine.

32:44.337 --> 32:45.922
Let me know when he reschedules.

32:46.006 --> 32:47.007
Sure.

32:47.549 --> 32:49.426
-I'll change out of this.
-Sure.

32:49.509 --> 32:50.594
[clears throat]

32:52.637 --> 32:53.805
What's that?

32:54.222 --> 32:55.348
[Meri] This?

32:55.432 --> 32:57.434
It's the mascot I'll be showing
at the presentation.

32:57.976 --> 32:59.102
-A mascot?
-That's right.

32:59.186 --> 33:03.773
I'm making one so I can promote the brand
on your website and online stores.

33:04.649 --> 33:06.610
-Would you like to see it?
-Sure.

33:06.693 --> 33:07.694
Just a second.

33:09.613 --> 33:11.198
I'll bring my laptop.

33:14.951 --> 33:16.786
[character grunting]

33:17.996 --> 33:19.706
It's not your money. Is that it?

33:20.665 --> 33:22.959
I can't even put it down
as a business expense.

33:24.294 --> 33:25.295
[scoffs]

33:26.338 --> 33:28.798
Are you and the victim
trying to steal from me?

33:28.882 --> 33:31.760
I had to pay him a lot
because there was a security footage.

33:31.843 --> 33:33.011
A security footage?

33:36.556 --> 33:37.641
[sighs]

33:39.184 --> 33:41.186
What about my father? What did he say?

33:41.269 --> 33:44.397
As far as he knows, you're the victim.

33:45.649 --> 33:46.858
To sell the story,

33:47.567 --> 33:49.736
you should stay hospitalized
for a few days.

33:51.238 --> 33:52.781
[sighs in exasperation]

33:52.864 --> 33:55.200
I'm bored out of my mind.

33:57.953 --> 33:59.079
[sighs]

33:59.704 --> 34:01.539
Get me some sushi, will you?

34:05.168 --> 34:06.962
I'm hungry, damn it!

34:08.546 --> 34:10.090
[♪ tense pulsing music playing]

34:26.064 --> 34:29.317
[Meri] I went with a cute image
that seemed to bring good luck.

34:29.401 --> 34:31.069
Her name is Myungsoon.

34:31.152 --> 34:33.905
I was thinking of adding her
to the online purchase page.

34:33.989 --> 34:35.198
I like it.

34:36.157 --> 34:37.701
[chuckles] Who's he?

34:37.784 --> 34:39.035
He's Myungsik.

34:39.119 --> 34:41.288
-Myungsoon's bestie.
-[acknowledges]

34:41.413 --> 34:42.497
They look alike.

34:42.580 --> 34:44.499
No, he resembles someone else.

34:45.292 --> 34:46.584
Who?

34:46.668 --> 34:47.877
My first love as a kid.

34:47.961 --> 34:50.380
What? Was he that ugly?

34:50.463 --> 34:52.257
Did you say he was ugly?

34:53.133 --> 34:55.510
He looks cute with those sparkling eyes.

34:55.593 --> 34:57.137
How can you think he's cute?

34:57.220 --> 34:59.598
He looks like
a pompous little troublemaker.

34:59.681 --> 35:01.057
That's part of his charm.

35:03.518 --> 35:06.521
Are you still in touch with Myungsik?

35:06.605 --> 35:08.231
My first love?

35:08.315 --> 35:09.649
Of course not.

35:09.733 --> 35:10.984
That was a long time ago.

35:11.443 --> 35:13.320
Do you also remember your first love?

35:13.695 --> 35:16.323
[inhales sharply] I'm not sure. [exhales]

35:16.406 --> 35:18.992
I haven't experienced love yet.

35:19.075 --> 35:21.411
You liar.

35:22.537 --> 35:24.039
[♪ whimsical music playing]

35:25.206 --> 35:26.207
I'm sorry.

35:26.750 --> 35:27.834
[chuckles]

35:29.127 --> 35:30.128
What was that?

35:30.712 --> 35:32.756
I threw it a bit too hard, didn't I?

35:32.839 --> 35:34.674
-[chuckling] I mean...
-[phone vibrating]

35:34.758 --> 35:36.301
-Sorry about that.
-Hold on.

35:36.801 --> 35:37.886
[line ringing]

35:38.762 --> 35:40.722
Hey, Wooju. Where are you?

35:41.181 --> 35:42.265
Oh, of course.

35:42.349 --> 35:43.975
When did we agree to meet again?

35:46.603 --> 35:48.063
Aren't you on your way over?

35:48.146 --> 35:49.356
I'm not.

35:49.439 --> 35:51.066
I'll head out right now.

35:51.149 --> 35:52.692
Right.

35:55.820 --> 35:57.697
Actually, it's fine.

35:58.073 --> 35:59.783
What can you do when you're busy?

36:02.243 --> 36:06.081
Actually, my senior asked me
to cover an on-call shift,

36:06.164 --> 36:08.208
so I'm calling to cancel.

36:09.084 --> 36:10.960
I'm the one who's sorry.

36:11.044 --> 36:12.921
I'll make it up to you with a meal.

36:14.255 --> 36:16.591
Sure, I'm being called right now.

36:16.675 --> 36:18.510
Bye. Sure thing.

36:19.302 --> 36:20.345
[line disconnects]

36:22.514 --> 36:23.890
[sighs sheepishly]

36:28.436 --> 36:30.522
Maybe I should've said I'd wait.

36:32.232 --> 36:34.109
[♪ gentle pop music playing over speakers]

36:37.445 --> 36:38.571
[sighs]

36:48.915 --> 36:50.041
Welcome.

36:50.709 --> 36:52.752
I'll have your strongest drink.

36:52.836 --> 36:53.962
Got it.

36:55.547 --> 36:56.589
[sighs softly]

36:58.675 --> 36:59.676
Seriously.

36:59.759 --> 37:02.429
Why did I pretend I was busy?

37:02.512 --> 37:03.513
[groans softly]

37:03.596 --> 37:04.597
Damn.

37:05.181 --> 37:07.684
[exclaims] You're such a loser.

37:11.146 --> 37:12.272
[exclaims quizzically]

37:14.232 --> 37:15.734
[♪ melancholy music playing]

37:24.325 --> 37:25.702
[♪ melancholy music fades]

37:26.578 --> 37:28.455
[♪ soft jazz music
playing over speakers]

37:38.381 --> 37:40.008
[exhales sharply]

37:40.091 --> 37:41.176
[exclaims]

37:41.259 --> 37:42.469
[breathes heavily]

37:47.515 --> 37:48.558
[clears throat]

37:51.060 --> 37:52.604
Making a living is no joke.

37:55.231 --> 37:57.066
Being an employee is tough.

37:57.150 --> 37:59.027
But all we can do is tough it out.

38:01.196 --> 38:03.698
That VIP patient you work for.

38:03.782 --> 38:06.409
Rumor has already spread about
what an ass he is.

38:07.869 --> 38:09.954
He's faking an injury
just to stay hospitalized.

38:11.748 --> 38:13.792
Still, you handled him gracefully.

38:13.875 --> 38:15.251
I have mad respect.

38:15.794 --> 38:17.128
Do I know you?

38:21.925 --> 38:23.343
It's me.

38:23.426 --> 38:26.012
We ran into each other
earlier at the hospital.

38:26.095 --> 38:27.096
I'm the doctor.

38:27.180 --> 38:30.558
-Who's been saying those things?
-What?

38:31.226 --> 38:32.310
They should be fired.

38:32.769 --> 38:35.563
The huge donation to the cancer center
was made in return for silence.

38:35.647 --> 38:36.648
Hold on.

38:36.731 --> 38:38.900
You got it all wrong.

38:38.983 --> 38:41.820
I only brought it up to comfort you,

38:41.903 --> 38:44.614
as I'm just an employee myself.

38:44.697 --> 38:47.200
Unsolicited words of comfort
are just arrogance.

38:48.618 --> 38:49.828
I apologize.

39:00.129 --> 39:01.130
Hold on.

39:01.881 --> 39:04.217
Why twist what I meant
when I was trying to be nice?

39:04.300 --> 39:06.052
It's not like I talked badly about anyone.

39:06.553 --> 39:08.054
[exclaims in realization]

39:08.137 --> 39:11.182
Are you telling me to shut up
since you spent the money?

39:12.058 --> 39:14.561
You seem to think money solves everything,

39:14.644 --> 39:16.855
but there's more to it than that.

39:16.938 --> 39:18.398
It's simpler this way.

39:19.524 --> 39:21.150
Work only as much as you're paid

39:21.901 --> 39:23.653
and stay just as quiet.

39:23.736 --> 39:24.737
[inhales deeply]

39:24.821 --> 39:27.115
That way, no one will be drained
for no reason.

39:27.198 --> 39:30.368
How can people live
without draining themselves emotionally?

39:32.829 --> 39:34.080
If you're upset,

39:34.163 --> 39:38.209
open up and let others comfort you
instead of acting tough.

39:39.419 --> 39:42.922
Why would you be drinking here
if you weren't upset?

39:43.006 --> 39:46.342
Who drinks alone like this
when they're not upset,

39:46.426 --> 39:47.677
like I am?

39:48.720 --> 39:50.430
[♪ upbeat whimsical music playing]

39:53.933 --> 39:55.768
[stutters] What is it?

39:55.852 --> 39:57.103
What?

39:57.729 --> 39:58.771
What is it?

39:59.522 --> 40:04.110
Do you think I'm drowning my sorrows
because a guy stood me up?

40:05.153 --> 40:06.362
I'm not.

40:09.699 --> 40:11.784
Excuse me, can I get a refill?

40:11.868 --> 40:12.994
[bartender] Sure thing.

40:16.789 --> 40:18.583
[♪ upbeat jazz music playing]

40:32.388 --> 40:34.515
Are you trying to flirt with me?

40:34.599 --> 40:36.392
I'm telling you to drink up and go.

40:36.976 --> 40:38.061
I'd rather drink in peace.

40:42.023 --> 40:43.274
[Jingyeong sighs]

40:44.108 --> 40:45.193
Here you go.

40:50.657 --> 40:51.783
[satisfied exhale]

40:51.866 --> 40:55.286
FROM YEOSU TO GANGNAM

40:55.370 --> 40:57.246
[automated voice] Ladies and gentlemen,

40:57.330 --> 41:00.124
we will soon arrive in Gangnam,
our destination.

41:00.208 --> 41:02.377
Please check if you have left
any luggage behind.

41:08.800 --> 41:10.426
[grunts, panting]

41:16.265 --> 41:17.558
[Kim Wooju] With this renewal,

41:17.642 --> 41:21.854
we hope to strengthen our brand identity
across all customer demographics.

41:21.938 --> 41:23.439
PACKAGE RENEWAL STATUS UPDATE

41:23.523 --> 41:26.776
The new packaging design
will be used on small gift packages,

41:26.859 --> 41:30.697
our website's purchase pages,
and gift features on social media.

41:31.322 --> 41:37.537
We hope the new mascot in the design
will help attract a younger customer base.

41:38.079 --> 41:39.330
There are ads on social media,

41:39.747 --> 41:42.375
plus vouchers and coupons, but...

41:42.458 --> 41:43.543
[Mom] I'm in Seoul.

41:43.626 --> 41:47.338
I made some side dishes,
so I'll drop by your in-laws' place.

41:47.422 --> 41:48.840
[Meri] My in-laws?

41:48.923 --> 41:51.926
[Kim Wooju] ...we look forward
to greater brand familiarity

41:52.010 --> 41:53.928
and increased attention on...

41:54.012 --> 41:55.471
[♪ gripping whimsical music playing]

41:58.349 --> 41:59.600
...on online platforms.

42:01.269 --> 42:02.270
Let's dive in.

42:02.353 --> 42:06.149
2025 MYUNGSOONDANG LEADERSHIP
ESSENTIAL ACADEMY

42:06.232 --> 42:07.734
Why aren't you picking up?

42:07.817 --> 42:08.818
MOM

42:15.158 --> 42:17.618
Goodness me. Hello.

42:20.204 --> 42:21.247
[exhales]

42:22.623 --> 42:24.625
Oh dear, I can't have this spilling.

42:24.709 --> 42:27.545
MERI

42:27.628 --> 42:30.089
[automated voice] The call
cannot be connected. Transferring to...

42:30.423 --> 42:31.674
[line ringing]

42:31.758 --> 42:33.384
Is something up?

42:33.468 --> 42:34.927
You're up soon.

42:35.887 --> 42:39.974
My mom's in Seoul and heading to Wooju's.

42:41.350 --> 42:42.602
[exclaims in realization]

42:43.394 --> 42:44.979
She doesn't know yet, does she?

42:46.647 --> 42:47.940
[hums thoughtfully]

42:49.025 --> 42:51.152
Ms. Yoo, you're up next.

42:51.235 --> 42:52.320
I'll be right there.

42:54.405 --> 42:57.867
Then, text me Mr. Kim's address.

42:57.950 --> 43:00.870
I'll go there and try to stop your mom.

43:00.953 --> 43:02.205
You give the presentation.

43:03.039 --> 43:04.791
-Don't worry.
-But...

43:04.874 --> 43:06.292
Go on.

43:07.251 --> 43:10.088
Thank you so much
for doing me this huge favor.

43:12.965 --> 43:14.300
[hums thoughtfully]

43:17.053 --> 43:18.346
The wedding is off?

43:18.429 --> 43:19.514
[sighs]

43:19.597 --> 43:21.724
What a joke of a family.

43:21.808 --> 43:24.143
Don't you and your daughter talk?

43:24.602 --> 43:26.354
It was called off ages ago.

43:26.437 --> 43:27.438
Wait.

43:27.980 --> 43:30.358
[chuckles nervously]
What do you mean it was called off?

43:30.441 --> 43:32.026
This is news to me.

43:32.110 --> 43:34.612
If you have any questions,
talk to your daughter.

43:34.695 --> 43:36.364
We've got nothing more to say.

43:37.115 --> 43:38.324
Hold on.

43:39.075 --> 43:42.662
Ms. Chun, don't be like this.

43:42.745 --> 43:45.206
They probably argued a little,

43:45.289 --> 43:48.668
but that's common for couples
before getting married.

43:48.751 --> 43:52.588
If Meri did something wrong,
I'll set her straight.

43:52.672 --> 43:55.174
A wedding isn't something
to play around with.

43:55.258 --> 43:56.509
[chuckles]

43:56.592 --> 43:59.720
Ms. Chun, why don't you cool off
and take this?

43:59.804 --> 44:02.849
I made you
some of the side dishes you love.

44:03.224 --> 44:04.559
There's green onion kimchi.

44:04.642 --> 44:05.643
Here.

44:07.645 --> 44:08.646
[hesitates]

44:08.813 --> 44:09.814
You shouldn't have.

44:10.273 --> 44:11.357
Seriously?

44:11.440 --> 44:13.234
It'd be rude to turn this down.

44:16.237 --> 44:17.697
[♪ gripping dramatic music playing]

44:18.906 --> 44:21.284
[GPS] You're almost at your destination.

44:28.249 --> 44:30.042
Look here, Ms. Oh.

44:30.126 --> 44:32.086
I say this because I feel bad for you.

44:32.170 --> 44:33.880
This isn't a lovers' spat.

44:33.963 --> 44:35.256
It's over between them.

44:35.673 --> 44:37.216
You know how your daughter is.

44:37.300 --> 44:38.593
She's vicious and nasty.

44:39.427 --> 44:41.596
No guy would be able to handle her.

44:41.679 --> 44:45.808
She had the audacity to snap back at me
with her eyes glaring.

44:45.892 --> 44:47.935
You should've taught her better.

44:48.436 --> 44:51.147
It would've been a mistake
to let her into this family.

44:51.230 --> 44:53.107
I thank our ancestors
for watching over us.

44:53.191 --> 44:54.275
Hallelujah.

44:54.984 --> 44:57.653
Anyway, if you have any decency,

44:57.737 --> 45:00.323
don't marry her off
until she grows as a person.

45:00.406 --> 45:03.159
Don't try to mess up my son's life again,

45:03.242 --> 45:04.994
and stay away.

45:05.453 --> 45:09.624
Oh, come on.
There's obviously a misunderstanding.

45:09.707 --> 45:10.750
Goodness me.

45:10.833 --> 45:11.834
Ms. Chun, wait.

45:11.918 --> 45:13.044
Please don't do this.

45:13.127 --> 45:15.171
Stop being such a loser.

45:16.422 --> 45:17.548
My goodness!

45:21.385 --> 45:22.511
[grunts]

45:25.181 --> 45:26.641
Unbelievable.

45:28.142 --> 45:29.268
[gasps]

45:29.560 --> 45:31.062
My green onion kimchi!

45:31.145 --> 45:32.146
I'm sorry.

45:33.105 --> 45:34.315
[♪ melancholy music playing]

45:34.398 --> 45:35.441
[sighs wearily]

45:36.234 --> 45:37.568
Oh, what do I do?

45:38.402 --> 45:39.445
[tires screech]

45:43.574 --> 45:45.076
Goodness me.

45:45.534 --> 45:47.870
My goodness.

45:47.954 --> 45:48.955
Are you all right?

45:49.038 --> 45:50.706
Yes, I'm fine.

45:51.374 --> 45:54.210
No, please leave it there.
I'll clean it up.

45:54.794 --> 45:55.795
It's fine.

45:55.878 --> 45:58.214
Goodness me, how can I ever thank you?

45:58.297 --> 45:59.924
Please, just stop.

46:00.007 --> 46:01.259
Your hands will stink.

46:01.342 --> 46:03.094
-Your hands will stink.
-Thank you.

46:03.970 --> 46:05.096
[sighs wearily]

46:06.097 --> 46:07.807
Are you Ms. Yoo's mother?

46:09.684 --> 46:10.851
Who are...

46:11.310 --> 46:12.561
[chuckles softly]

46:12.645 --> 46:13.813
[exclaims softly]

46:22.363 --> 46:23.447
[hesitates]

46:23.906 --> 46:27.702
So, you work with Meri's company?

46:27.785 --> 46:29.078
That's right.

46:29.578 --> 46:32.832
Something urgent came up,
so she asked for a favor.

46:32.915 --> 46:35.209
I'm supposed to drive you
to the bus terminal.

46:36.377 --> 46:38.838
Anyway, feel free to talk to me casually.

46:40.381 --> 46:42.300
Still, you're a team leader.

46:42.925 --> 46:44.719
Ms. Yoo is the head of her company.

46:45.970 --> 46:47.388
Well, you're not wrong.

46:47.471 --> 46:49.098
[chuckling]

46:49.807 --> 46:52.143
Anyway, has Meri been doing a good job?

46:52.226 --> 46:53.519
Of course.

46:53.602 --> 46:56.355
She's so vital to this project
that I came here instead of her.

46:56.439 --> 46:58.691
She's giving an important presentation
to the chairwoman.

46:58.774 --> 46:59.775
Goodness.

47:00.192 --> 47:03.279
She gives one mean presentation.

47:04.280 --> 47:05.740
You know,

47:05.823 --> 47:09.410
even as a little girl,
she was bold and outspoken.

47:09.493 --> 47:13.414
Her drawings were so good
that she won an award from the governor.

47:13.497 --> 47:17.043
In school, she always led
the art projects. [chuckles]

47:17.418 --> 47:18.836
You must've been proud of her.

47:18.919 --> 47:20.463
Of course, I was.

47:21.714 --> 47:23.382
Well...

47:23.841 --> 47:26.469
I don't know if you heard them earlier,

47:26.552 --> 47:30.848
but Meri's not as prickly
as she comes across.

47:30.931 --> 47:33.225
She's as feminine as it gets.

47:33.809 --> 47:37.396
She gives everything she has
to the people she adores.

47:37.480 --> 47:38.564
[smacks lips]

47:38.647 --> 47:40.566
After her father passed,

47:40.649 --> 47:43.194
she had to step up
as the man of the house.

47:43.277 --> 47:46.530
Supporting herself through college
and living away from home

47:46.614 --> 47:48.199
made her tougher,

47:48.282 --> 47:51.577
and I'm worried people
might misunderstand her.

47:51.660 --> 47:53.245
That's not the case.

47:53.829 --> 47:55.956
Everyone likes Ms. Yoo.

47:56.040 --> 47:58.376
She's cheerful and skilled at her job.

47:58.751 --> 48:00.086
[chuckles]

48:00.169 --> 48:03.297
She's naturally cheerful and hardworking.

48:03.381 --> 48:06.384
Do you want to know what happened
when she was a kid?

48:07.051 --> 48:09.428
Goodness me. I'm blabbering to a stranger.

48:10.012 --> 48:11.180
-[both chuckle]
-Oh, dear.

48:11.931 --> 48:14.141
Can I continue?

48:14.225 --> 48:15.226
Of course.

48:15.309 --> 48:19.397
She was little at the time,
not even 100cm tall.

48:19.480 --> 48:20.481
She was 99cm.

48:21.190 --> 48:25.736
And I was in bed
aching all over with the flu.

48:25.820 --> 48:28.572
Her dad had just started out
as a taxi driver and...

48:36.414 --> 48:38.833
-Can you wrap things up?
-You should hurry out.

48:41.127 --> 48:42.378
[line ringing]

48:43.838 --> 48:44.922
Goodness.

48:45.005 --> 48:48.342
Why would you come here
when I'm leaving soon?

48:50.636 --> 48:51.720
[exclaims quizzically]

48:53.180 --> 48:54.348
At Wooju's place?

48:55.224 --> 48:58.227
I wasn't able to meet his mother.

48:58.310 --> 49:00.062
She wasn't home.

49:00.146 --> 49:01.147
Whatever.

49:01.230 --> 49:03.315
I couldn't get in touch with her,
so I left.

49:03.399 --> 49:05.568
You shouldn't have dropped by unannounced.

49:05.651 --> 49:07.570
Call ahead next time.

49:07.653 --> 49:09.405
I got it.

49:09.488 --> 49:11.198
Who? The team leader?

49:11.282 --> 49:12.283
Goodness.

49:12.366 --> 49:14.493
He's the one who drove me
to the bus terminal.

49:14.577 --> 49:16.412
Make sure to thank him.

49:16.495 --> 49:18.247
Sure, go about your day.

49:18.747 --> 49:20.916
-[line disconnects]
-You can get on the bus.

49:21.000 --> 49:23.377
I could've gotten the ticket myself,
and now I feel bad.

49:23.461 --> 49:25.713
Don't be. Ms. Yoo asked me to.

49:25.796 --> 49:27.339
[chuckles] Sure.

49:29.049 --> 49:30.426
By the way...

49:32.344 --> 49:35.890
Don't tell Meri about what happened today.

49:36.807 --> 49:39.727
I'm sure she didn't tell me for a reason.

49:40.144 --> 49:43.147
What's done is done,
so why push her for answers?

49:43.230 --> 49:44.940
She's probably feeling even worse.

49:46.066 --> 49:47.067
Sure.

49:48.360 --> 49:50.529
[station announcer]
The bus for Yeosu will soon depart.

49:51.238 --> 49:53.073
-Please board.
-I should get going.

49:54.241 --> 49:55.534
[chuckles softly]

49:55.618 --> 49:57.620
Visit Yeosu sometime.

49:58.037 --> 49:59.663
I'll treat you to a tasty meal.

50:00.789 --> 50:01.999
-Sure.
-All right.

50:02.500 --> 50:03.501
Get going.

50:03.584 --> 50:05.252
[♪ slow, pleasant music playing]

50:09.006 --> 50:10.382
Get going already.

50:16.263 --> 50:17.765
[Kim Wooju] Your mother just left.

50:18.349 --> 50:20.351
I stayed until her bus pulled away.

50:20.434 --> 50:22.728
I'm on my way to your place right now.

50:24.855 --> 50:26.774
Your mother asked me
to drop off a few things.

50:28.359 --> 50:30.402
I'll wait for you at home, then.

50:31.320 --> 50:32.321
Sure.

50:35.157 --> 50:36.242
[line disconnects]

50:36.909 --> 50:37.993
[sighs]

50:42.498 --> 50:44.166
[phone vibrating]

50:44.750 --> 50:46.085
WOOJU'S SISTER

50:50.589 --> 50:51.590
[sighs]

50:58.097 --> 50:59.139
Hello?

51:02.643 --> 51:04.186
[♪ melancholy music playing]

51:22.121 --> 51:23.289
[doorbell rings]

51:35.759 --> 51:36.802
[Wooju sighs]

51:37.720 --> 51:39.513
-Here.
-Oh, thanks.

51:40.306 --> 51:42.349
They should go straight into the fridge.

51:42.433 --> 51:43.434
Right.

51:44.893 --> 51:46.270
Is something up?

51:47.021 --> 51:48.314
Gosh, no. [sniffles]

51:49.148 --> 51:52.359
The tension's finally leaving
now that the presentation's done.

51:54.528 --> 51:55.613
Thank you for today.

51:55.696 --> 51:57.948
I was able to finish it well,
thanks to you.

51:58.032 --> 51:59.825
[chuckles] So I heard.

52:02.077 --> 52:03.329
Are you sure you're okay?

52:03.954 --> 52:05.873
You don't seem well.

52:08.709 --> 52:09.752
[sniffles]

52:09.835 --> 52:11.712
Sorry about this. [chuckles softly]

52:14.465 --> 52:15.591
I'll take that.

52:19.219 --> 52:20.638
My mom...

52:23.432 --> 52:24.933
found out.

52:26.894 --> 52:28.520
WOOJU'S SISTER

52:28.604 --> 52:29.772
[sighs]

52:33.192 --> 52:34.777
-Hello?
-[angrily] You!

52:35.527 --> 52:37.237
How could you not have told your mom yet?

52:37.321 --> 52:39.281
You've got a lot of nerve.

52:39.365 --> 52:41.700
Your mom came by our house!

52:41.784 --> 52:46.872
My mom had to rest
after the shock your mom caused!

52:52.127 --> 52:53.545
I'm dying.

52:53.629 --> 52:55.547
This is killing me.

52:56.215 --> 52:58.801
[sighs] This is exactly
why I didn't tell her.

52:58.884 --> 52:59.968
[sniffles]

53:01.637 --> 53:03.597
I was fine with it all,

53:04.973 --> 53:06.600
but I knew my mom...

53:07.726 --> 53:11.563
[sniffles] I knew my mom would be upset.

53:20.197 --> 53:21.198
[sniffles]

53:21.281 --> 53:22.908
I should've been there.

53:25.035 --> 53:28.539
If I were there,
it would've been a fair fight.

53:29.415 --> 53:31.375
I bet my mom couldn't even get a word in.

53:34.169 --> 53:37.172
Then, why don't you bring it up with her?

53:37.631 --> 53:39.258
She'll soon find out anyway.

53:39.341 --> 53:41.885
What can I say, considering what happened?

53:44.805 --> 53:45.889
[sighs wearily]

53:45.973 --> 53:49.476
I became a divorcée
without ever having a wedding.

53:50.978 --> 53:53.522
She won't be proud of me anymore.

53:54.523 --> 53:55.524
Come on.

53:56.316 --> 53:58.819
Why do you always have to be
her pride and joy?

53:59.820 --> 54:02.322
What more do you have to be
besides her daughter?

54:03.657 --> 54:05.242
Don't worry about it too much.

54:05.743 --> 54:11.165
Besides, I think she's ready to hear
your side of the story.

54:18.338 --> 54:20.966
MOM

54:26.430 --> 54:27.514
[line ringing]

54:28.182 --> 54:29.266
[inhales sharply]

54:31.643 --> 54:33.270
[phone ringing]

54:34.229 --> 54:35.898
MERI

54:39.443 --> 54:40.527
[sighs]

54:41.987 --> 54:42.988
Mom.

54:46.241 --> 54:47.326
I have...

54:49.077 --> 54:50.621
-something to tell you.
-Meri.

54:51.914 --> 54:53.582
Just forget about it all.

54:53.665 --> 54:55.417
He's not the only man out there.

54:55.834 --> 54:58.086
I only approved because you liked him.

54:58.170 --> 54:59.713
To be honest,

55:00.714 --> 55:02.758
I was never fond of that punk.

55:02.841 --> 55:03.967
[smacks lips]

55:04.051 --> 55:08.514
They say you need to clear out the junk
to make room for something better,

55:08.597 --> 55:11.099
so forget about him and live your life.

55:12.226 --> 55:13.268
Mom.

55:15.562 --> 55:16.813
I'm sorry.

55:16.897 --> 55:19.691
What are you apologizing for?

55:20.067 --> 55:22.528
Do better and show him what he's missing.

55:22.611 --> 55:24.780
You already have a place to live,

55:24.863 --> 55:28.033
so move on
if someone better comes your way.

55:29.660 --> 55:30.827
[exclaims quizzically]

55:31.161 --> 55:32.412
You moved?

55:32.913 --> 55:33.956
To where?

55:40.295 --> 55:41.463
[breath trembling]

55:42.589 --> 55:43.966
You won a prize?

55:44.967 --> 55:46.510
[stutters] What...

55:47.427 --> 55:49.054
What exactly did you win?

55:50.806 --> 55:53.100
Wooju doesn't know.

55:54.351 --> 55:55.894
Of course, I tried calling him.

55:55.978 --> 55:57.563
I tried over and over.

55:57.646 --> 55:59.773
What can I do when he won't pick up?

55:59.856 --> 56:01.316
All right.

56:03.068 --> 56:06.613
Meri, listen to me loud and clear.

56:11.118 --> 56:12.160
You...

56:12.578 --> 56:15.914
No matter what, don't get caught.

56:15.998 --> 56:17.791
-[♪ dramatic music playing]
-[exclaims quizzically]

56:18.292 --> 56:20.460
Are you sure I should keep this up?

56:21.753 --> 56:23.213
What if I get caught?

56:23.297 --> 56:25.757
You should make sure no one finds out.

56:25.841 --> 56:27.676
Always watch what you say.

56:29.052 --> 56:30.053
Meri,

56:31.138 --> 56:32.472
stay strong.

56:32.556 --> 56:33.849
Sure.

56:34.391 --> 56:35.392
Got it.

56:36.184 --> 56:37.603
Don't worry.

56:38.645 --> 56:39.646
Right.

56:40.522 --> 56:41.565
Sure.

56:43.692 --> 56:44.776
[line disconnects]

56:48.614 --> 56:49.740
[sighs]

56:50.032 --> 56:51.158
What the heck?

56:53.744 --> 56:55.495
Who knew Mom was so cool?

56:56.663 --> 56:59.958
The world isn't as harsh
as you might imagine.

57:05.213 --> 57:06.214
You?

57:07.382 --> 57:09.801
You threw your own happiness away.

57:09.885 --> 57:11.720
[♪ gripping comical music playing]

57:13.138 --> 57:16.016
That's karma at work.

57:19.561 --> 57:20.562
My gosh.

57:22.147 --> 57:24.733
You know what this is?

57:25.692 --> 57:27.527
It's amor fati.

57:27.611 --> 57:28.820
[firework whistles]

57:29.655 --> 57:31.490
[singing]
♪ Amor fati ♪

57:31.573 --> 57:33.116
[sings happily]

57:35.702 --> 57:37.704
-♪ Amor fati ♪
-[Meri] But sometimes,

57:37.788 --> 57:39.873
the least expected also happens.

57:39.956 --> 57:41.291
[♪ jazz music playing over speakers]

57:41.375 --> 57:43.293
I've never had meat this tender before.

57:43.377 --> 57:44.461
[giggles]

57:45.212 --> 57:46.296
Baby, have some.

57:46.755 --> 57:47.756
Thanks.

57:47.839 --> 57:49.216
-Dig in, too.
-Sure.

57:49.299 --> 57:50.550
[phone vibrating]

57:56.515 --> 57:57.516
[chuckles softly]

57:58.684 --> 58:00.686
Baby, what's after dinner?

58:01.353 --> 58:02.354
Why do you ask?

58:02.437 --> 58:04.940
A friend's in the neighborhood,
so I thought we'd meet up.

58:05.524 --> 58:07.317
A friend? Who?

58:07.401 --> 58:09.152
A school friend who lives close by.

58:09.236 --> 58:10.529
I'll make introductions later.

58:12.698 --> 58:15.325
-Sure, got it.
-Hmm.

58:18.495 --> 58:19.496
[clears throat]

58:19.871 --> 58:20.872
Sure thing.

58:22.124 --> 58:23.125
[elevator dings]

58:25.585 --> 58:27.295
-See you later.
-See you later.

58:29.297 --> 58:30.465
[whispers] I love you.

58:30.549 --> 58:31.550
[whispers] I love you, too.

58:32.968 --> 58:35.095
-Don't be gone for too long.
-Got it.

58:36.888 --> 58:38.432
[♪ tense foreboding music playing]

58:40.350 --> 58:41.351
Damn it.

58:41.435 --> 58:43.687
Hurry!

58:43.770 --> 58:44.855
[elevator dings]

58:58.243 --> 58:59.244
[woman screams]

59:02.831 --> 59:03.874
[exclaims]

59:06.001 --> 59:07.127
[elevator dings]

59:08.044 --> 59:09.629
See you soon.

59:11.214 --> 59:12.257
[line disconnects]

59:13.759 --> 59:14.801
[panting]

59:19.306 --> 59:20.348
[exclaims softly]

59:25.020 --> 59:26.354
Which floor?

59:26.730 --> 59:28.315
[breathing heavily]

59:29.316 --> 59:30.692
Shit.

59:34.738 --> 59:35.822
1 UNREAD MESSAGE

59:35.906 --> 59:37.741
C: I'M IN ROOM 3613

59:38.158 --> 59:40.035
Room 3613.

59:43.663 --> 59:44.790
Why won't it work?

59:46.500 --> 59:47.876
The hotel key card.

59:49.336 --> 59:50.879
Come on. [breath trembling]

59:51.379 --> 59:53.340
Why won't it work?

59:53.423 --> 59:54.883
Come on.

59:55.550 --> 59:57.552
Damn it!

01:00:00.138 --> 01:00:01.348
[elevator dings]

01:00:01.640 --> 01:00:03.016
[♪ dramatic sting]

01:00:08.355 --> 01:00:09.397
[exclaims]

01:00:09.481 --> 01:00:10.816
[♪ foreboding music playing]

01:00:12.692 --> 01:00:13.985
[in English] Sorry.

01:00:16.154 --> 01:00:17.280
[in Korean] Shit.

01:00:28.208 --> 01:00:29.209
Shit.

01:00:34.381 --> 01:00:35.799
[panting]

01:00:41.388 --> 01:00:43.014
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:00:43.098 --> 01:00:44.140
Jenny?

01:00:46.184 --> 01:00:47.185
Jenny...

01:00:51.189 --> 01:00:52.399
[continues panting]

01:00:52.691 --> 01:00:53.775
[doorbell chiming]

01:01:04.411 --> 01:01:05.954
-Baby.
-Babe.

01:01:06.454 --> 01:01:08.123
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

01:01:38.194 --> 01:01:40.947
Wow, she made so much food.

01:01:45.452 --> 01:01:48.371
Always so generous, isn't she?

01:01:51.291 --> 01:01:52.417
[hums softly]

01:02:00.467 --> 01:02:02.177
[exclaims] It's so good.

01:02:04.262 --> 01:02:05.805
MOM

01:02:11.269 --> 01:02:12.687
Hey, Mom. What's up?

01:02:13.396 --> 01:02:14.564
Unbelievable.

01:02:15.190 --> 01:02:17.859
I've looked everywhere.

01:02:18.485 --> 01:02:20.028
It isn't in any of my pockets.

01:02:20.528 --> 01:02:23.990
No way. I didn't even pull
my wallet out on the bus.

01:02:25.533 --> 01:02:26.576
Goodness.

01:02:27.202 --> 01:02:28.203
You know what?

01:02:28.787 --> 01:02:31.539
I must have dropped it there.

01:02:32.832 --> 01:02:34.167
In Mr. Kim's car?

01:02:35.460 --> 01:02:37.420
Sure, I'll ask.

01:02:37.963 --> 01:02:39.089
Got it.

01:02:40.548 --> 01:02:41.675
[line disconnects]

01:02:43.051 --> 01:02:44.219
TEAM LEADER KIM WOOJU

01:02:45.261 --> 01:02:46.429
[line ringing]

01:02:48.264 --> 01:02:49.975
A black folding wallet?

01:02:50.642 --> 01:02:51.643
I'll look for it.

01:02:52.060 --> 01:02:53.061
Sure.

01:02:53.603 --> 01:02:54.604
[line disconnects]

01:03:04.572 --> 01:03:05.573
[grunts]

01:03:12.163 --> 01:03:13.707
Why did I miss this?

01:03:14.082 --> 01:03:15.166
OH YOUNGSOOK

01:03:25.593 --> 01:03:29.305
-[♪ enchanting music playing]
-Sometimes, the thing you're searching for

01:03:30.223 --> 01:03:31.933
is right under your nose.

01:03:38.023 --> 01:03:39.149
Seriously?

01:03:55.040 --> 01:03:56.708
YOUNGSOOK'S RESTAURANT

01:03:59.169 --> 01:04:00.587
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

01:04:00.670 --> 01:04:04.966
[teddy] Enough with the tears,
or the tiger will come and get you.

01:04:05.050 --> 01:04:06.760
Take it.

01:04:07.260 --> 01:04:09.345
My dad gave it to me as a birthday gift.

01:04:20.690 --> 01:04:22.442
The girl I'd been looking for

01:04:23.318 --> 01:04:24.694
was right under my nose.

01:04:28.948 --> 01:04:30.158
[chuckles softly]

01:04:30.784 --> 01:04:33.536
I wonder if she knew.

01:04:33.620 --> 01:04:35.163
[♪ poignant, melancholy music continues]

01:04:42.212 --> 01:04:43.546
[tires screech, car horn blaring]

01:04:46.841 --> 01:04:47.926
[truck horn blaring]

01:04:48.009 --> 01:04:49.135
[car horn continues blaring]

01:04:50.220 --> 01:04:51.596
[tires screeching]

01:04:52.889 --> 01:04:53.973
[tires screech]

01:04:54.057 --> 01:04:55.517
[♪ melancholy music playing]

01:05:05.068 --> 01:05:06.361
[student in English] Are you okay?

01:05:06.861 --> 01:05:07.946
Are you okay?

01:05:08.029 --> 01:05:13.076
[Kim Wooju] That when harsh winds
swept through my lonely heart...

01:05:13.159 --> 01:05:14.160
[student] Oh, no.

01:05:16.496 --> 01:05:19.749
...the warmth from a girl
I'd just met brought me...

01:05:19.833 --> 01:05:21.084
[teddy] Enough with the tears,

01:05:21.167 --> 01:05:24.379
-[Kim Wooju] ...a brief moment of peace.
-or the tiger will come and get you.

01:05:24.712 --> 01:05:26.381
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

01:05:28.174 --> 01:05:30.802
Who will take care of him?

01:05:31.719 --> 01:05:34.389
That poor boy!

01:05:42.021 --> 01:05:44.899
[Kim Wooju] She cried for me.

01:05:45.358 --> 01:05:48.570
Could you perhaps stop by just this once?

01:05:49.737 --> 01:05:50.738
MUTE

01:05:50.822 --> 01:05:52.282
[laughing softly]

01:05:53.992 --> 01:05:55.285
When I met her again,

01:05:56.035 --> 01:05:57.120
I wanted to say

01:05:57.412 --> 01:05:58.413
[clears throat]

01:05:58.496 --> 01:05:59.664
how grateful I was.

01:06:00.623 --> 01:06:01.666
[clears throat]

01:06:03.710 --> 01:06:04.711
Hold on.

01:06:04.794 --> 01:06:06.421
What are you doing this weekend?

01:06:06.880 --> 01:06:09.549
Shouldn't you have
a wedding photo or something?

01:06:09.632 --> 01:06:11.092
That'd lower his suspicion.

01:06:11.718 --> 01:06:13.636
He was clearly suspicious last time.

01:06:13.720 --> 01:06:15.054
With you gone...

01:06:15.138 --> 01:06:16.264
He's watching us.

01:06:17.307 --> 01:06:18.808
-He really is.
-[chuckles softly]

01:06:19.934 --> 01:06:21.561
Everyone likes Ms. Yoo.

01:06:21.644 --> 01:06:23.646
She's cheerful and skilled at her job.

01:06:23.730 --> 01:06:25.064
[chuckles]

01:06:25.148 --> 01:06:28.109
She's naturally cheerful and hardworking.

01:06:28.193 --> 01:06:29.277
Do you want to know...

01:06:29.360 --> 01:06:31.237
[Kim Wooju] But I never asked

01:06:31.863 --> 01:06:33.740
if she remembered me.

01:06:36.701 --> 01:06:38.244
This was enough distance.

01:06:38.786 --> 01:06:40.205
I was repaying the favor

01:06:41.247 --> 01:06:43.416
by helping her this much.

01:06:49.464 --> 01:06:50.965
[♪ pleasant, upbeat music playing]

01:07:12.237 --> 01:07:13.529
[phone vibrating]

01:07:19.160 --> 01:07:20.620
Hey, did you find it?

01:07:20.703 --> 01:07:21.704
[Wooju] It's me.

01:07:23.498 --> 01:07:24.582
How have you been?

01:07:25.583 --> 01:07:27.335
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

01:08:05.748 --> 01:08:08.501
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:08:08.584 --> 01:08:11.087
[Meri] I'm supposed to work
with Managing Director Baek?

01:08:11.170 --> 01:08:13.548
[Kim Wooju] Call me three times a day,
no exceptions.

01:08:13.631 --> 01:08:15.591
[Wooju] I'm choosing you, Meri.

01:08:15.675 --> 01:08:18.177
[Jingyeong] Who could possibly
save you, Wooju?

01:08:18.261 --> 01:08:19.929
There's no need to look very far.

01:08:20.013 --> 01:08:22.223
[Eungsoo's mom] He's lucky
he wasn't kicked out of the family.

01:08:22.307 --> 01:08:24.892
[Kim Wooju] My parents passed away
on my birthday,

01:08:25.601 --> 01:08:26.602
and it was my fault.

01:08:26.686 --> 01:08:28.896
[Wooju] The house is that punk's,
isn't it?

01:08:28.980 --> 01:08:31.441
[Meri] Didn't you say to team up
with Wooju if push came to shove?

01:08:31.524 --> 01:08:33.359
[Kim Wooju] Maybe it's because I like you.

01:08:33.443 --> 01:08:35.361
I don't like seeing you with another guy.

01:08:35.445 --> 01:08:37.530
Does it bother you that I like you?

01:08:38.489 --> 01:08:39.615
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

01:08:41.826 --> 01:08:43.828
Translated by Hyelim Park
